WHY THIS LICENCE, AND NOT A SOFTWARE ONE

Of the 42,832,472 bytes in fly-doctrines.odmod, 42,820,374 are
data/brain.odfly: the FlyWire connectome, packed. The mod is overwhelmingly
somebody else's measurement of a fly, and FlyWire publishes its released data
under CC BY-NC 4.0. Licensing the parts separately would mean a package whose
dominant component is CC BY-NC sitting under a notice that says otherwise, so
the whole thing takes the data's terms.

It also matches the game: OpenDoctrines ships under the OpenDoctrines
Non-Commercial License, so nothing here is more permissive than the thing it
plugs into.

CC licences are written for works rather than for software, and that is a real
mismatch for src/*.c. It is the lesser problem. A mod that redistributes 42 MB
of CC BY-NC data under a permissive software licence would be making a promise
about that data which is not the author's to make.

WHAT IS COVERED

  data/brain.odfly, and the copy inside fly-doctrines.odmod
      The FlyWire connectome, packed into this project's format. Not
      originally this project's work. See ATTRIBUTION.

  src/, tools/, build.sh, MANIFEST.json, README.md
      Written for this project, offered under the same terms.

ATTRIBUTION, which CC BY-NC requires

The connectome:

    FlyWire -- https://flywire.ai
    Dorkenwald et al., "Neuronal wiring diagram of an adult brain",
    Nature (2024).

The model this simulation implements:

    Shiu, P.K., Sterne, G.R., Spiller, N. et al. "A leaky integrate-and-fire
    computational model based on the connectome of the entire adult
    Drosophila brain reveals insights into sensorimotor processing",
    Nature (2024).

FlyWire's own citation guidance is at https://flywire.ai/guidelines and takes
precedence over this paragraph if the two ever disagree.

NON-COMMERCIAL

CC BY-NC 4.0 permits sharing and adaptation but not commercial use. Running the
mod, modifying it, and redistributing it are fine. Selling it, or bundling it
into something sold, is not.
